  "description": "Compute forward pass of transformer decoder layer featuring autoregressive causal masking and encoder-decoder cross-attention.\n\nCausal masking sets attention scores of future positions to -inf, ensuring position i cannot attend to positions j > i during autoregressive generation.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\n\\mathbf{h}_1 = \\mathbf{x} + \\text{CausalSelfAttn}(\\mathbf{x}), \\quad \\mathbf{h}_2 = \\mathbf{h}_1 + \\text{CrossAttn}(\\mathbf{h}_1, \\mathbf{M})\n$$\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n1. Apply causally masked self-attention to input sequence x and add residual connection\n2. Apply cross-attention attending to encoder memory M and add residual connection\n3. Return activated representation matrix rounded to 4 decimal places\n\n### Returns\nNested 2D list of shape (N, D) representing decoder block activations.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: Transformer Decoder Block\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\nNeural networks achieve their remarkable expressive power by stacking linear layers interspersed with non-linear activation functions and normalization layers. Without non-linear activations, any deep network would collapse into a single shallow linear regression. **Transformer Decoder Block** ensures signals propagate cleanly through dozens or hundreds of layers without vanishing or exploding.\n\nCausal masking sets attention scores of future positions to -inf, ensuring position i cannot attend to positions j > i during autoregressive generation. In this problem, the goal is to: compute forward pass of transformer decoder layer featuring autoregressive causal masking and encoder-decoder cross-attention.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe core governing equation for this operation is:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{h}_1 = \\mathbf{x} + \\text{CausalSelfAttn}(\\mathbf{x}), \\quad \\mathbf{h}_2 = \\mathbf{h}_1 + \\text{CrossAttn}(\\mathbf{h}_1, \\mathbf{M})\n$$\n\nEvery term in this formulation plays a precise mathematical role in ensuring dimensional consistency, numerical stability, and correct algorithmic behavior.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1**: Apply causally masked self-attention to input sequence x and add residual connection\n2. **Phase 2**: Apply cross-attention attending to encoder memory M and add residual connection\n3. **Phase 3**: Return activated representation matrix rounded to 4 decimal places\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Gradient Flow**: Carefully designed activation functions (like ReLU, GELU, and Swish) maintain strong gradient signals during backpropagation.\n* **Internal Covariate Shift**: Normalization techniques (like LayerNorm and RMSNorm) standardize hidden states across channels or batch dimensions, allowing models to train stably at higher learning rates.\n* **Hardware Friendly**: Modern deep learning frameworks implement these layers using fused GPU kernels to reduce memory round-trips.",
