  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Transformer Decoder Block** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport torch, math\n\ndef dl_decoder_block(x: list, memory: list, W_mask_qkv: list = None, W_cross_qkv: list = None) -> list:\n    t_x, t_mem = torch.tensor(x, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(memory, dtype=torch.float32)\n    N, D = t_x.shape\n    i = torch.arange(N).unsqueeze(1)\n    j = torch.arange(N).unsqueeze(0)\n    mask = torch.where(j > i, float('-inf'), 0.0)\n    h1 = t_x + torch.matmul(torch.softmax(torch.matmul(t_x, t_x.transpose(-2, -1)) / math.sqrt(D) + mask, dim=-1), t_x)\n    h2 = h1 + torch.matmul(torch.softmax(torch.matmul(h1, t_mem.transpose(-2, -1)) / math.sqrt(D), dim=-1), t_mem)\n    return torch.round(h2, decimals=4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
